{"id":"chatcmpl-00800a7f-626e-4ada-aa60-28acce3d7722","object":"chat.completion","created":1795230194,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-heavy visual QA workflow for medical imaging where laterality is ambiguous due to projection type. The strategy combines expert visual QA, targeted region-of-interest zooming, and explicit uncertainty verification before committing to a forced-choice answer. When verification flags ambiguity, the pattern is to re-query the expert with more specific anatomical reasoning rather than abandoning the best estimate.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a visual finding's laterality or identity is ambiguous due to projection/orientation, query an expert tool first, then zoom into the relevant region to gather corroborating visual evidence.\",\n    \"Use a verification step to surface uncertainty explicitly, then re-query the expert with sharper anatomical/contextual constraints instead of guessing blindly.\",\n    \"Anchor ambiguous spatial judgments to orientation markers and anatomical landmarks (spine, sternum, side markers) rather than raw pixel position.\",\n    \"For forced-choice tasks with imperfect evidence, converge on the answer most consistently supported across expert queries and document the reasoning basis.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Combine expert visual QA with ROI zoom on the region of interest; always cross-check laterality against orientation markers and anatomical landmarks.\",\n    \"Ambiguity resolution\": \"When verification flags uncertainty, escalate to a more specific expert query with explicit anatomical constraints rather than accepting the first answer.\",\n    \"Forced-choice decision making\": \"Gather multiple independent expert signals; if they converge, commit with documented rationale even when single-view evidence is imperfect.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the orientation marker (e.g., 'L') and anatomical landmarks before asserting laterality.\",\n    \"After any verification flag, re-query the expert with sharper constraints and check for consistency across responses before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":721,"total_tokens":1094,"completion_tokens":373,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":721},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":373}}}